meta {
  name: Set club quota
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/clubs/{{clubId}}/quota
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{bullBoardUser}}
  password: {{bullBoardPassword}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "limit": 250
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.quota.limit: eq 250
}

docs {
  Operator only. Uses the same Basic auth as Bull Board (`BULL_BOARD_USER` / `BULL_BOARD_PASSWORD`), which now guards everything under `/admin`. A Bearer token, even a club admin's, gets 401.

  `limit` is a whole number from 0 to 1,000,000. Setting it below `used` is allowed and simply stops further downloads (`remaining: 0`). `used` is never changed here.

  | Status | Code | When |
  |---|---|---|
  | 200 | | limit changed |
  | 400 | `VALIDATION_ERROR` | `limit` missing, negative, fractional, a string, or too big |
  | 401 | `UNAUTHORIZED` | missing or wrong credentials |
  | 404 | `CLUB_NOT_FOUND` | no such club |
  | 429 | `RATE_LIMITED` | 10 wrong passwords in 15 minutes (only 401s count) |

  Example response:

  ```json
  {
    "quota": {
      "limit": 250,
      "used": 0,
      "remaining": 250,
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-19T10:53:10.735Z"
    }
  }
  ```
}
